.po 0.55i
.ll 7.15i
.ps 10.3
.vs 12.8
.fam H
.ce
.ft B
Detailed Qwen vs Llama Query, DAG, and SPARQL Comparison Report
.br
.ft R
.ce
Files used: Pipeline_Retest_Report_qwen_all.csv and Pipeline_Retest_Report_llama_all.csv
.br
.ce
Report date: 10 June 2026
.br
.sp
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
1. Executive Summary
.br
.ft R
This report uses only the two retest CSV files supplied by the user. It compares final
.br
answer correctness, likely wrong MATCH labels, DAG/operator sequence quality, SPARQL
.br
generation quality, scan reliability, and per-query winners.
.br
Main conclusion: Qwen is stronger overall. It has many more MATCH answers, many more
.br
MATCH+PARTIAL answers, better head-to-head answer results, and better SPARQL/scan
.br
reliability. Llama has a few individual wins but is mostly weaker in this retest.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
2. Answer Correctness Counts
.br
.ft R
Qwen: total 142; MATCH 52 (36.6%); PARTIAL 23 (16.2%); MISMATCH 60 (42.3%); CRASH 7
.br
(4.9%); MATCH+PARTIAL 75 (52.8%).
.br
Llama: total 143; MATCH 12 (8.4%); PARTIAL 13 (9.1%); MISMATCH 112 (78.3%); CRASH 6
.br
(4.2%); MATCH+PARTIAL 25 (17.5%).
.br
Head-to-head on shared question occurrences:
.br
- Tie: 76 (53.5%)
.br
- Qwen: 62 (43.7%)
.br
- Llama: 4 (2.8%)
.br
Status pair counts:
.br
- Qwen MISMATCH vs Llama MISMATCH: 58
.br
- Qwen MATCH vs Llama MISMATCH: 30
.br
- Qwen PARTIAL vs Llama MISMATCH: 21
.br
- Qwen MATCH vs Llama MATCH: 12
.br
- Qwen MATCH vs Llama PARTIAL: 10
.br
- Qwen CRASH vs Llama CRASH: 4
.br
- Qwen CRASH vs Llama MISMATCH: 3
.br
- Qwen PARTIAL vs Llama PARTIAL: 2
.br
- Qwen MISMATCH vs Llama CRASH: 1
.br
- Qwen MISMATCH vs Llama PARTIAL: 1
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
3. Checking Whether MATCH Is Actually Correct
.br
.ft R
I created a per-query audit CSV. For JSON/numeric ground truths, expected values must
.br
appear in the answer or scan raw rows. For no-data ground truths, answers must clearly
.br
say no data/no rows/no rule. Zero answers for no-data ground truth are marked
.br
NEEDS_REVIEW because zero is only safe for count questions.
.br
Qwen audit verdicts: WRONG=64, CORRECT=26, UNDER_LABELLED=14, PARTIAL_OR_WRONG=13,
.br
PARTIAL_OK=13, NEEDS_REVIEW=12
.br
Llama audit verdicts: WRONG=115, CORRECT=11, NEEDS_REVIEW=9, UNDER_LABELLED=4,
.br
PARTIAL_OR_WRONG=3, PARTIAL_OK=1
.br
Potential wrong/review MATCH labels found: 27 total. These rows are listed in
.br
Detailed_Qwen_vs_Llama_Per_Query_Audit.csv.
.br
Review example (Qwen): Across the entire investor database, how many Gold holdings does
.br
investor INV-005 hold? | GT: There is no data in raw_data_sample to answer this query. |
.br
Answer: Investor INV-005 holds 0 Gold holdings. | Audit: NEEDS_REVIEW.
.br
Review example (Qwen): Across the entire investor database, how many investors affected
.br
by the Interest Rate Hike scenario have a ... | GT: There is no business rule/data to
.br
calculate this from raw_data_sample. | Answer: No investors affected by the Interest
.br
Rate Hike scenario have a Moderate portfolio health status. | Audit: WRONG.
.br
Review example (Qwen): Can you tell me what the average holding duration in days for
.br
investor INV-012? | GT: There is no data in raw_data_sample to answer this query. |
.br
Answer: A database error prevented data retrieval. | Audit: WRONG.
.br
Review example (Qwen): Can you tell me what the total current value of ETF holdings for
.br
investor INV-010? | GT: There is no data in raw_data_sample to answer this query. |
.br
Answer: The total current value of ETF holdings for investor INV-010 is 0. | Audit:
.br
NEEDS_REVIEW.
.br
Review example (Qwen): Could you show me total Lump Sum investments made per investor
.br
across all time.? | GT: (no rows returned) | Answer: Deepak Sharma has made total Lump
.br
Sum investments of 35656852 across all time. | Audit: WRONG.
.br
Review example (Qwen): How many Redemption transactions has investor INV-008 made? | GT:
.br
There is no data in raw_data_sample to answer this query. | Answer: Investor INV-008 has
.br
made 0 Redemption transactions. | Audit: NEEDS_REVIEW.
.br
Review example (Qwen): How many holdings does investor INV-015 have in total? | GT:
.br
There is no data in raw_data_sample to answer this query. | Answer: Investor INV-015 has
.br
a total of 0 holdings. | Audit: NEEDS_REVIEW.
.br
Review example (Qwen): How many investors affected by the Interest Rate Hike scenario
.br
have an At Risk portfolio health status? | GT: There is no business rule/data to
.br
calculate this from raw_data_sample. | Answer: No investors affected by the Interest
.br
Rate Hike scenario have an At Risk portfolio health status. | Audit: WRONG.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
4. DAG / Operator Sequence Strength
.br
.ft R
DAG quality was scored simply: one point each for Retrieve, Generate, Scan, Validate,
.br
and Explain appearing in the planned sequence. This checks pipeline completeness, not
.br
semantic correctness.
.br
Qwen: average DAG completeness score 4.81/5.
.br
Llama: average DAG completeness score 4.86/5.
.br
DAG head-to-head winner Tie: 139 (97.9%)
.br
DAG head-to-head winner Llama: 3 (2.1%)
.br
Interpretation: both models usually create plausible DAGs. Qwen does not win by DAG
.br
shape alone; it wins because its generated query and answer survive later stages more
.br
often.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
5. SPARQL / Scan Generation Strength
.br
.ft R
SPARQL quality was scored from generated query presence, SELECT/PREFIX shape, scan
.br
success, no unknown terms, and scan error absence. This captures practical query
.br
generation quality better than DAG shape alone.
.br
Qwen: average SPARQL/scan score 4.32/5; scan success 117; scan error 18; rows with
.br
unknown terms 15.
.br
Llama: average SPARQL/scan score 2.67/5; scan success 60; scan error 77; rows with
.br
unknown terms 78.
.br
SPARQL head-to-head winner Qwen: 79 (55.6%)
.br
SPARQL head-to-head winner Tie: 53 (37.3%)
.br
SPARQL head-to-head winner Llama: 10 (7.0%)
.br
Interpretation: Qwen is much stronger at producing SPARQL that reaches scan success.
.br
Llama has many more scan errors and many more rows with unknown RDF terms.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
6. Failure Pattern Comparison
.br
.ft R
Qwen failure stages: blank=67, Validate=51, Scan=17, Exception=7
.br
Llama failure stages: Scan=55, Validate=49, blank=33, Exception=6
.br
Qwen failures are often validation-stage or specific crashes. Llama failures are more
.br
heavily scan-stage, meaning the generated SPARQL often cannot execute correctly against
.br
the graph.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
7. Variant / Repeated Query Check
.br
.ft R
Qwen: 12 exact repeated questions, 12 extra repeated rows, 0 repeated questions with
.br
mixed statuses.
.br
Llama: 12 exact repeated questions, 12 extra repeated rows, 0 repeated questions with
.br
mixed statuses.
.br
Repeated queries are internally consistent within each model, but Qwen and Llama often
.br
differ on the same repeated query.
.br
.sp
.ne 5
.ft B
